{% doc %}
  @prompt
    Create a new custom testimonial section for the Shopify Horizon theme that closely matches the supplied reference design.
    
    SECTION STRUCTURE
    
    Create a full-width dark section containing two equal-width cards in a two-column desktop layout.
    
    Use a centered container with:
    
    * Maximum width: 1600px
    * Horizontal page padding: 16px on desktop and 12px on mobile
    * Gap between cards: 24px
    * Card corner radius: 32px
    * Section background: #050505
    
    LEFT INTRODUCTION CARD
    
    Use a dark charcoal background: #121212.
    
    At the top, include:
    
    * A small outlined pill badge
    * An editable star icon
    * Editable badge text, default: “Technology”
    * Large editable heading, default: “Building high-performance Shopify experiences with AI-driven innovation”
    * Editable description below the heading
    
    At the bottom of the card, include two editable statistics displayed side by side:
    
    Statistic one:
    
    * Value: “3000+”
    * Label: “Shopify Projects Delivered”
    
    Statistic two:
    
    * Value: “98%”
    * Label: “Client Satisfaction Rate”
    
    Use white for the heading, light grey for the body content, muted grey for statistic labels, and orange #FF7417 for the statistic values.
    
    RIGHT TESTIMONIAL CARD
    
    Use a deep navy background: #08233F.
    
    Create a testimonial carousel with exactly 10 editable testimonial blocks. Each block must include:
    
    * Optional client image
    * Circular fallback profile icon when no image is uploaded
    * Client name
    * Client role or company
    * Testimonial text
    * Large decorative quotation mark in the upper-right corner
    
    Display only one testimonial at a time.
    
    Add circular previous and next arrow buttons at the bottom center. The buttons must move through all 10 testimonials and loop continuously from the last testimonial back to the first.
    
    Add these optional section settings:
    
    * Enable or disable autoplay
    * Autoplay speed from 3 to 10 seconds
    * Show or hide testimonial counter
    * Show or hide client images
    
    Pause autoplay when the user hovers over the card, focuses on a control, or interacts with the carousel. Support horizontal swipe gestures on mobile. Disable autoplay when the visitor has reduced-motion enabled.
    
    THEME EDITOR SETTINGS
    
    Make the following editable in the Shopify theme editor:
    
    * Badge text
    * Heading
    * Description
    * Both statistic values and labels
    * All 10 testimonials
    * Client images
    * Client names
    * Roles or companies
    * Testimonial quotes
    * Section background color
    * Introduction card color
    * Testimonial card color
    * Heading color
    * Body color
    * Muted text color
    * Accent color
    * Testimonial text colors
    * Maximum content width
    * Card gap
    * Card radius
    * Top and bottom spacing
    * Autoplay
    * Autoplay speed
    * Testimonial counter
    * Client images
    
    RESPONSIVE BEHAVIOUR
    
    On desktop, show both cards next to each other at equal widths and equal heights.
    
    On tablets and mobile devices, stack the introduction card above the testimonial card. Keep comfortable spacing, readable typography, and touch-friendly arrow buttons.
    
    Use fluid typography with clamp() so the heading and testimonial text resize smoothly. Prevent horizontal overflow on smaller screens.
    
    TECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS
    
    Build this as a self-contained Shopify Liquid section compatible with the Horizon theme.
    
    Use:
    
    * Shopify section schema
    * A maximum of 10 testimonial blocks
    * Vanilla JavaScript only
    * Scoped CSS using section.id
    * Semantic HTML
    * Accessible button labels
    * aria-live for changing testimonials
    * block.shopify_attributes for theme-editor block selection
    * No external libraries or dependencies
    
    Include 10 editable sample testimonial blocks in the section preset so the section is populated immediately when added through the theme editor.
    , Update the existing testimonial section in my Shopify Horizon theme. Do not create a new section and do not change the left introduction card. Only fix the right testimonial card.
    
    1. FIX THE CLIENT IMAGE/LOGO
    
    The uploaded client images or company logos are currently not appearing. The section is displaying the generic profile icon instead.
    
    For every testimonial block:
    
    * Keep an editable Shopify image-picker setting named “Client image or logo.”
    * Render the selected image using Shopify’s image_url and image_tag filters.
    * Display the fallback profile icon only when no image has been uploaded.
    * Ensure the uploaded image is not hidden by CSS, opacity, positioning, overflow, or incorrect conditional Liquid logic.
    * Give the image container a fixed size of approximately 56–64px.
    * Use object-fit: contain so transparent logos are completely visible and not cropped.
    * Add 6–8px internal padding for company logos.
    * Use a subtle translucent background behind transparent logos.
    * Keep the image sharp by requesting an image width of at least 200px.
    * Add a setting that lets the merchant choose between “Logo” and “Profile image.”
    * For “Logo,” use object-fit: contain with a softly rounded container.
    * For “Profile image,” use object-fit: cover with a circular container.
    
    Use this Liquid rendering logic:
    
    {% if block.settings.client_image != blank %}
    {{
    block.settings.client_image
    | image_url: width: 240
    | image_tag:
    loading: 'lazy',
    widths: '80, 120, 160, 240',
    alt: block.settings.name
    }}
    {% else %}
    Display the fallback profile SVG icon
    {% endif %}
    
    2. REMOVE THE EMPTY UPPER SPACE
    
    The top-left area of the navy testimonial card currently looks empty. Reorganize the testimonial content to use this space properly.
    
    Use this content order:
    
    * Client image or company logo at the top-left
    * Client name and role beside the image
    * Decorative quotation-mark icon at the top-right
    * Testimonial quote immediately below the client information
    * Navigation arrows and slide counter at the bottom center
    
    Place the complete author row near the top of the card with approximately 40–48px top padding. Do not vertically center the testimonial content and do not leave a large empty gap above it.
    
    The spacing should be:
    
    * 16px between the client image and client information
    * 28–36px between the author row and testimonial quote
    * Controls positioned at the bottom using margin-top: auto
    * No artificial min-height or large top margin on the quote
    * No justify-content: space-around or space-evenly
    
    Use this layout approach:
    
    * Testimonial card: display flex, flex-direction column
    * Testimonial content stays aligned to flex-start
    * Author row appears at the top
    * Quote follows directly after the author row
    * Navigation controls use margin-top: auto
    * Keep enough bottom padding around the controls
    
    3. VISUAL RESULT
    
    The right card should feel balanced and intentional:
    
    * Uploaded client logo/image clearly visible at the top-left
    * Name and company details beside it
    * Quote icon aligned at the top-right
    * Testimonial content starts higher inside the card
    * No empty area where indicated in the reference screenshot
    * Navigation remains centered at the bottom
    * Maintain the existing deep navy background, typography, rounded corners, 10 testimonial blocks, autoplay, swipe interaction, counter, and arrow navigation
    
    4. RESPONSIVE BEHAVIOUR
    
    On mobile:
    
    * Keep the image/logo, name, and role aligned in one compact author row
    * Reduce the logo/image size to approximately 50–54px
    * Keep the quote icon visible without overlapping the author information
    * Reduce internal card padding to approximately 24px
    * Keep the quote directly below the author row
    * Ensure uploaded logos remain completely visible and are not cropped
    
    Do not remove any existing testimonial blocks or theme-editor settings. Preserve all 10 testimonials and only correct the image rendering, content order, and spacing.
    , Update the existing testimonial section in my Shopify Horizon theme. Do not create a new section and do not change the left introduction card. Improve only the right testimonial slider.
    
    Each of the 10 testimonial blocks must have these editable fields:
    
    1. Client image or company logo
    2. Reviewer or company name
    3. Optional job title or company details
    4. Review date
    5. Quality of work rating from 1 to 5
    6. Communication rating from 1 to 5
    7. Full testimonial text
    8. Service reviewed
    
    RIGHT TESTIMONIAL CARD LAYOUT
    
    Use the following content order to remove the empty space:
    
    Top row:
    
    * Display the uploaded client image or company logo on the left.
    * Show the reviewer or company name beside the image.
    * Show optional job title or company information below the name.
    * Display the review date on the top-right.
    * Keep a large, subtle decorative quotation mark in the upper-right background without overlapping the date.
    
    Ratings area:
    
    Directly below the top row, show two separate rating rows:
    
    * “Quality of work” followed by five star icons and the numeric rating
    * “Communication” followed by five star icons and the numeric rating
    
    Use filled gold stars for the selected rating and muted outlined stars for the remaining rating. Use gold #F5B942 for active stars.
    
    Review content:
    
    * Display the full testimonial beneath the ratings.
    * Use readable white or very light grey text.
    * Do not make the testimonial overly italic.
    * Use approximately 20–24px desktop text with comfortable line height.
    * Keep the review aligned to the left.
    
    Service information:
    
    At the bottom of the testimonial content, display:
    
    “Service reviewed: [service name]”
    
    Make “Service reviewed:” slightly muted or semibold and make the service name clearly readable.
    
    EXAMPLE FIRST TESTIMONIAL
    
    Populate the first testimonial block with:
    
    Client/company name: Champ Water
    
    Review date: Jun 25, 2026
    
    Quality of work: 5 out of 5
    
    Communication: 5 out of 5
    
    Testimonial:
    
    “The Root Syntax Team was phenomenal with their quick communication and attention to detail by working with us to ensure that we were happy with the finished product. I highly recommend them to any business who needs a website built.”
    
    Service reviewed: Store build or redesign
    
    IMAGE AND LOGO FIX
    
    The uploaded client image or logo must display correctly.
    
    * Add an image-picker setting to every testimonial block.
    * Render the selected image using Shopify image_url and image_tag filters.
    * Display the fallback profile icon only when no image has been uploaded.
    * Do not allow CSS, opacity, positioning, or incorrect Liquid conditions to hide the image.
    * Add a “Logo” or “Profile image” display option.
    * For a company logo, use object-fit: contain with 6–8px padding.
    * For a profile image, use object-fit: cover and a circular shape.
    * Use a 56–64px image container on desktop and 50–54px on mobile.
    * Use a subtle translucent background behind transparent logos.
    * Request an image width of at least 200px so it remains sharp.
    
    Use this Liquid logic:
    
    {% if block.settings.client_image != blank %}
    {{
    block.settings.client_image
    | image_url: width: 240
    | image_tag:
    loading: 'lazy',
    widths: '80, 120, 160, 240',
    alt: block.settings.reviewer_name
    }}
    {% else %}
    Display the fallback profile SVG icon
    {% endif %}
    
    SPACING AND ALIGNMENT
    
    Do not vertically center the testimonial information.
    
    * Keep all review content aligned near the top of the navy card.
    * Use 40–48px internal padding on desktop.
    * Use 20–24px between the top identity row and ratings.
    * Use 24–30px between the ratings and review text.
    * Use 20–24px between the review and service information.
    * Position navigation controls at the bottom using margin-top: auto.
    * Do not use large top margins, space-around, or space-evenly.
    * Remove the large empty area previously visible above the testimonial.
    
    SLIDER REQUIREMENTS
    
    Preserve all 10 editable testimonial blocks.
    
    Keep:
    
    * Previous and next circular arrows
    * Slide counter such as “3 / 10”
    * Autoplay option
    * Editable autoplay speed
    * Continuous looping
    * Mobile swipe gestures
    * Pause on hover
    * Reduced-motion accessibility
    * block.shopify_attributes support
    
    THEME-EDITOR SETTINGS FOR EACH TESTIMONIAL
    
    Add these block settings:
    
    * image_picker: Client image or logo
    * select: Image type — Logo or Profile image
    * text: Reviewer or company name
    * text: Role or company details
    * text: Review date
    * range: Quality of work rating, minimum 1 and maximum 5
    * range: Communication rating, minimum 1 and maximum 5
    * textarea: Testimonial
    * text: Service reviewed
    
    RESPONSIVE BEHAVIOUR
    
    On mobile:
    
    * Stack the identity information and date cleanly if there is not enough width.
    * Keep the client logo or image visible.
    * Keep both rating rows readable and aligned.
    * Reduce the testimonial text size appropriately.
    * Keep the service information above the navigation controls.
    * Use approximately 24px card padding.
    * Prevent text, stars, date, or logo from overlapping.
    
